{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>The families of the sons of Kohath shall encamp … southward.</b> And adjacent to them was the standard of Reuben, who encamped southward — woe to the wicked, woe to his neighbor. Therefore Dathan and Abiram suffered, and two hundred and fifty men with Korah and his assembly, for they were drawn along with them in their dispute (Tanchuma)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:15.257138764Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}